# Vercel uploads the repo, then runs `vercel.json`'s buildCommand against it.
# The static build needs `app/` and nothing else, so everything below is either
# rebuilt on the host, irrelevant to a browser bundle, or must never leave this
# machine.
#
# NOTE: writing this file replaces .gitignore as the CLI's ignore source, so the
# entries .gitignore already covers are repeated here on purpose.

# Rebuilt on the host by `npm ci` / `npm run build`.
node_modules
/dist
app/dist

# Local tenant state — never upload a database.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal
*.db
.env
/fleet.yaml
/fixture/state.json

# The CLI/server half of the repo. Not reachable from a static bundle, and the
# root install is skipped, so uploading it would only slow the deploy.
/src
/test
/scripts
/web
/gates
/reference
/docs
Dockerfile
fly.toml

# Working notes.
/.superpowers
/.claude
/PROGRESS.md
